MUSICAL TEMPERAMENT AS RAPIDITY LINEAR ALGEBRA
============================================================

  THE RAPIDITY BASIS:
  r_2 = ln(2)/2 = 0.3465735903  (octave)
  r_3 = ln(3)/2 = 0.5493061443  (twelfth)
  r_5 = ln(5)/2 = 0.8047189562
  r_7 = ln(7)/2 = 0.9729550745

IMPORTANT COMMAS (rapidity vectors close to zero)
--------------------------------------------------

  Comma                                Vector      Rapidity     Cents
  -----------------------------------------------------------------
  Pythagorean comma           [-19, 12, 0, 0]   +0.00677552    +23.46
  Syntonic comma               [-4, 4, -1, 0]   +0.00621126    +21.51
  Diesis (great)                [7, 0, -3, 0]   +0.01185826    +41.06
  Archytas comma               [6, -2, 0, -1]   +0.00787418    +27.26
  Septimal kleisma             [-5, 2, 2, -1]   +0.00222718     +7.71
  Schisma                      [-15, 8, 1, 0]   +0.00056426     +1.95
  Diaschisma                  [11, -4, -2, 0]   +0.00564700    +19.55
  Ragisma                      [-1, -7, 4, 1]   +0.00011430     +0.40

  Each comma is a VECTOR in the rapidity vector space R^primes.
  Small commas = vectors near the KERNEL of the 'tuning map'.
  Temperament = quotienting R^primes by the comma lattice.

============================================================
EQUAL TEMPERAMENT AS RAPIDITY QUOTIENT
============================================================

  12-TET: quotient by the Pythagorean comma [-19, 12, 0, 0].
  Identify r_3 with (19/12)*r_2.
  Then: fifth = r_3 - r_2 = (19/12 - 1)*r_2 = (7/12)*r_2.

  In 12-TET:
  semitone = r_2/12
  Intervals in semitones:
    unison          :  0 semitones = rapidity 0.000000
    minor 2nd       :  1 semitones = rapidity 0.028881
    major 2nd       :  2 semitones = rapidity 0.057762
    minor 3rd       :  3 semitones = rapidity 0.086643
    major 3rd       :  4 semitones = rapidity 0.115525
    perfect 4th     :  5 semitones = rapidity 0.144406
    tritone         :  6 semitones = rapidity 0.173287
    perfect 5th     :  7 semitones = rapidity 0.202168
    minor 6th       :  8 semitones = rapidity 0.231049
    major 6th       :  9 semitones = rapidity 0.259930
    minor 7th       : 10 semitones = rapidity 0.288811
    major 7th       : 11 semitones = rapidity 0.317692
    octave          : 12 semitones = rapidity 0.346574

============================================================
THE TOURNAMENT-MUSIC DICTIONARY
============================================================

  Every tournament quantity has a musical interpretation.

  TOURNAMENT            MUSIC                    RAPIDITY
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  H(T) = 1             silence (no vibration)    0
  H(T) = 3             T_3 cyclic tournament     0.549 = octave
  H(T) = 5             n=4 max                   0.805 ~ twelfth
  H(T) = 7             FORBIDDEN                 0.973 ~ 7th harm
  H(T) = 9             n=5 some                  1.099 ~ 2 octaves
  H(T) = 15            n=5 cyclic                1.354 ~ 9th harm
  H(T) = 21            FORBIDDEN                 1.522 ~ 11th harm
  H(T) = 189           Paley T_7 max             2.621 ~ 4th harm
  H(T) = 95095         Paley T_11 max            5.731 ~ 8th harm

  The forbidden values sit at the 7th and 11th harmonics!
  These are the LAST harmonics before the overtone series
  stops being 'musical' (11th harmonic = neutral fourth,
  considered dissonant in most Western traditions).

============================================================
THE RAPIDITY OF INTERVALS BETWEEN H-VALUES
============================================================

  The rapidity RATIO between successive Paley H-values:

  H(T_7)/H(T_3) = 189/3 = 63.0000
  rapidity of ratio = 2.071567
  = ln(189/3)/2 = 2.071567
  = 5.9773 octaves

  H(T_11)/H(T_7) = 95095/189 = 503.1481
  rapidity of ratio = 3.110442
  = ln(95095/189)/2 = 3.110442
  = 8.9748 octaves

